2026-09-07 STAGE 0 REDESIGN: same-phy EBUSY kills all TX.
Daemon proved it: `iw dev mon1 set channel 6 -> EBUSY (-16)`, TX self-test
0->0 STUCK, no-channel-line. Cause: mon1+wlan1 shared phy1; NM/wpa_supplicant
pins the phy, every channel set dies, hwsim tunes nothing, driver drops all
TX silently (socket-level success, tx_packets frozen). Same-phy sharing is
unworkable for injection. New layout (setup v2): mon1 ALONE on first hwsim
radio (free hopping), STA wlan1 (recreated) on second radio for NM, AP later
joins STA's phy (same channel by construction). Daemon unchanged (discovers
STA via /run/wifishim/sta_phy, mon by name). Also learned: ls-function breaks
bare `ls` (use `command ls`); multiline python -c breaks on fish (use files).
2026-09-07 STAGE 1 PROVEN: NM lists real phone-seen APs on wlan1, BOTH bands
(Elizabeth2/SmartRG 2.4GHz + High5 5GHz/ch153, correct BSSIDs/security).
Two lessons: (1) tx_packets NEVER counts monitor-injected TX on hwsim — the
self-test STUCK verdict was a false alarm from a bogus oracle; socket errors
are the only real failure signal (self-test reworded). (2) Single scans can
miss APs (hop/dwell rendezvous is probabilistic); repeats converge. Uniform
signal 84 on all entries = hwsim default for injected frames (cosmetic).
Remaining: Stage 2 open-network E2E (hostapd AP + dnsmasq + phone connect).

=== 2026-09-07 WPA2 "password incorrect" — three credential bugs fixed ===
SYMPTOM: NM connects, EAPOL fails, "password incorrect" despite right password.
(1) STALE SECRETS: serving key was UUID-only. NM saves the typed password
    AFTER profile creation, so first detection often sees empty/stale PSK;
    corrections never re-triggered bringup (hostapd kept the first secret
    forever). Fix: key = uuid + sha256(ssid/keymgmt/psk)[:16]; any secret
    change tears down + rebuilds hostapd.
(2) PASSPHRASE MANGLE: wpa_passphrase= raw line breaks on '#' (comment char),
    quotes, edge whitespace -> wrong PMK -> handshake fails. Fix: derive hex
    PSK via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA1 locally, write wpa_psk= (immune to all of it).
(3) MISSING NEIGHBOR PIN (designed, never coded): unicast DHCP OFFERs to a
    not-yet-owned address die in the neighbor queue (test/03 lesson). Fix:
    ip neigh replace <first-pool> lladdr <STA MAC> nud permanent on bringup.
ALSO: hostapd stdout/stderr now go to /run/wifishim/hostapd.log (was DEVNULL
— EAPOL failures were undebuggable); list-first BSSID lookup (full scan only
as fallback, saves ~15 s per activation); phone join attempts throttled to
1/SSID/2min (each flaps the phone uplink — was unbounded per 3 s poll).

=== 2026-09-07 orchestrator watched ap1 + hostapd reuse crash loop ===
SYMPTOM: orchestrator logged "watching NM wifi on ap1"; connects did nothing;
hostapd log spun "Match already configured" + AP-DISABLED forever.
ROOT CAUSE 1: STA discovery skipped mon*/lo but not ap*. Directory order made
it grab OUR OWN ap1 (same phy) instead of wlan1 — NM never activates there,
so detections never fired. Fix: exclude ap* in BOTH daemons' discovery.
ROOT CAUSE 2: ap1 reuse across bringups. First-ever hostapd run works; every
reuse dies EINVAL ("already configured") because teardown never reset the
iface type. Fix: bringup kills stale hostapd/dnsmasq (bracket-safe pkill),
deletes + recreates ap1 fresh, spoofs MAC, then starts hostapd.
ALSO: hostapd liveness gate via ctrl PONG before declaring serving (fail in
the retry loop, never serve dead). Phone leg untouched.

=== 2026-09-07 honesty guard: teardown on phone failure ===
OBSERVED: wrong password typed -> local EAPOL "succeeds" (same key both ends,
meaningless), real AP rejects phone -> user sees工作的假象 locally + auth
error on phone. Worst outcome: fake success.
FIX: phone_ensure records PHONE_OK[ssid]; main loop tears the AP side down on
False (NM shows honest DOWN, retries start a fresh cycle; phone attempts stay
throttled 1/SSID/2min). Suppression pins the exact failed config until it
changes or NM leaves. Also fixed style-flagged literal comparison via
membership form (del after acting, one-shot semantics).
TEST GUIDANCE: validate with a KNOWN password (High5: phone already there, no
uplink risk). Rapid clicking outruns 30 s phone joins; wait 60 s per attempt.

=== 2026-09-07 dual-band flip-flop + saved-password staleness ===
LOG PROOF: orchestrator served SmartRG as ch52/:67 (hostapd died instantly,
DFS radar channel) then ch6/:66 seconds later — phone scan returns whichever
BSS was heard last, and each rebuild flaps BSSID+channel mid-session.
FIX: per-SSID pinning (keep serving the same BSS while visible), preference
2.4 GHz > non-DFS 5 GHz > anything (loud WARN on DFS-only), RSSI tiebreak
(rssi added to parse output). Pin releases when the BSS vanishes.
SEPARATE ISSUE (user-side, not code): "saved password fails, fresh works" =
the NM profile holds a STALE/WRONG secret (typed once wrong, saved forever).
Fix from chair: delete the profile, retype carefully:
  nmcli connection delete "SmartRG-377e 4"
Serving-key content hash already rebuilds hostapd on secret change, and hex
PSK is special-char immune, so a careful retype converges.

=== 2026-09-07 band preference: 5 GHz default ===
Operator prefers 5 GHz (cleaner spectrum; High5 ch153 does 180 Mbps).
WIFISHIM_BAND_PREF env (5g default, 2.4 flips): non-DFS 5 first, then 2.4,
DFS/odd always last (hostapd dies on DFS regardless of preference — e.g.
SmartRG 5 GHz BSS on ch52 still correctly serves via 2.4 GHz ch6).
Pins are in-memory: daemon restart picks up the new policy immediately.

